  Why: 'Walls 000-022 (DeepShoreCliff, E/SE) are the harbour''s south arm. The deep water at their foot stays deep (the arrival is from the north-east); a stack and three skerries stand off the arm so the harbour reads as held between two arms. Its walls (PR 5w, by real id, clockwise): 000, 001, 002, 003, 004, 005, 006, 007, 008, 009, 010, 011, 012, 013, 014, 015, 016, 017, 018, 019, 020, 021, 022; part 2 drew it on walls 000-022. (terrain pass 9 part 2, p2_data.py sha256 15750c11...; PR 5w, on the ground file: paint only)'
